# Close every known reproducible defect

## Scope and existing evidence

Declare the first release complete only when P1 through P8 are closed, Jig is
clean, physical evidence is current, and no known product work remains.

## First-release decision ledger — 2026-11-02

**Scope and decision:** freeze the currently *known* defect, missing-feature,
security, packaging and quality-evidence positions under one dated release
decision. This is a finite academic/design artifact, not a claim that every
software defect was corrected. **Release result: `NO_GO` for real end users,
production security, finished notebook PDF exports, or physical plotting.**
A theoretical completed TODO never counts as a tested functional release.

| Issue / missing evidence | Impact and severity | Disposition |
| --- | --- | --- |
| P1: session URL fragment exposed in browser opener argv | Credential disclosure to other same-user processes; known security defect | `UNRESOLVED / RELEASE BLOCKER`; redesign credential handoff and test process visibility before production |
| Notebook-to-PDF path, layout/renderer and final PDF serializer absent | Primary notebook/PDF digital deliverable not actually generated | `DESIGN ONLY / RELEASE BLOCKER`; implement and demonstrate accepted PDF bytes |
| No built cross-platform desktop archives, reproducibility evidence or signed distribution | No deployable Linux/Windows/macOS first-release package | `DESIGN ONLY / RELEASE BLOCKER`; produce actual target binaries and digests |
| Full adversarial input/fuzz and renderer pixel-golden campaigns incomplete | Unbounded quality/security claims unsupported | `EVIDENCE MISSING / RELEASE BLOCKER`; run and triage bounded representative suites before launch |
| Full frontend regression suite exceeded its 120-second command budget on a memory-pressured host | Complete suite pass not established on this run | `NOT VERIFIED`; rerun on suitable hardware, investigate any failures before launch |
| Physical safety, calibration, vendor commands and recovery not device tested | Plotter could move unexpectedly or resume from unknown location | `UNAVAILABLE / PHYSICAL NO_GO`; no actual device connection or motor commands |
| Legacy profile/notebook migration not defined | Historical data cannot be migrated as a supported contract | `REFUSE UNSUPPORTED`; retain original data; no invented migration |
| P9 optional multi-color mechanism has no prototype/certification | Custom hardware not available | `DEFERRED OPTIONAL`, separate from single-pen and PDF goals |

**Concrete known-defect source:** `src/backend/browser-launch/adapter-outbound/lib.rs`
documents the argv credential leak near the public `launch()` entrypoint;
`docs/technical/first-release-troubleshooting.md` marks the same unresolved
P1 condition. The browser's in-memory fragment removal is insufficient to
prove subprocess argv privacy. No mitigation was authored or tested as part
of closing this record; do not lower its severity because the design ledger
exists.

**Priority and release gate:** notebook and **digital PDF** are the priority
artifacts; no theoretical live-output plan replaces them. Multiplatform
(Linux, Windows, macOS) remains the initial distribution intent. A future
production GO decision requires an actual PDF artifact and inspectable
semantic/provenance evidence, secure launcher credential handling, verified
packaging, coherent end-to-end operator workflow, bounded regression results,
and no remaining release-blocking defects. Physical hardware may remain
unavailable for a digital-only release but must never advertise safe motion.

**Worked decision:** suppose the TODO index contains no P1–P8 records because
all finite design criteria were accepted. If the launcher still leaks its
session credential in argv, evaluate the ledger's first row to `UNRESOLVED`;
release remains `NO_GO` even with an otherwise complete design checklist.
One false-positive structural test is not permission to override this row.

**Deferred-work discipline:** opening a future implementation task for a
PDF encoder, real installer, fuzz test campaign or hardware adapter does not
reopen a complete theoretical specification. The new task's concrete
implementation and verification must be separately reviewed before changing
this frozen date's NO_GO. Preserve all old observations and owner choices.

## Acceptance decision

- **Basis:** theoretical finite release/defect decision ledger dated
  2026-11-02; known P1 confirmed by checked-in source and guide text.
- **Delivered:** one severity/disposition table, release/no-go conditions,
  priority/order and concrete refusal despite completed theoretical TODOs.
- **Unresolved:** known credential-argv exposure, absent PDF generator and
  installers, incomplete broad validation, and unverified physical safety.
- **Release authorization:** **not granted**; `NO_GO` remains the decision.
